From 05081a8dd37e1249dedce48fa863cd8115ebebdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:56:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] jffs: no file or folder on /jffs stays writable by every user

Field (RT-BE88U, v3.4.7): 250+ files under /jffs were mode 0666 - SSH
authorized keys, VPN certificates and keys, ACME files, rule lists. The
v3.3.8 umask 022 shapes only NEW files; a rewrite keeps the old mode and
a backup restore untars the old modes. With a nobody-run daemon able to
write sshd_authkeys, that is a path to root.

shared/reaper_jfile.c reaper_jffs_perm_sweep(): an lstat walk of the
mount (same device, depth 32, regular files and folders only, sticky
folders kept) that clears only the other-write bit (0666 -> 0664). Called
from start_jffs2() and the ubifs mount right after setup_jffs_dirs(),
before anything runs from /jffs.

syslogd starts about 44 s later, so the sweep's result is logged by
reaper_jffs_perm_report() from init's START case right after
start_logger(), which also writes the boot record /tmp/reaper/jffs.sweep
("<changed> <failed>") for the diagnostics.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
